# ============================================================================
#  Vibes monorepo: root .gitignore
# ============================================================================
#
#  Layout:
#    commands/     personal CLI tools (bash, Python, Node)
#    linux-setup/  machine setup scripts + "pc" command center (Python/GTK)
#    tgdrive/      Telegram-backed drive (Python server, desktop app, web UI)
#
#  How this file is organised:
#    1. Generic sections by OS / editor / language. Most are defensive: they
#       cover tools this repo doesn't use yet, so a new project in any
#       language starts out clean.
#    2. Repo-specific rules for each project.
#    3. Re-includes (lines starting with "!"), at the very end so they win
#       over any broad rule above them.
#
#  Patterns deliberately left OUT, because they would hide real source here:
#    lib/     linux-setup/lib/ is shell source (the stock Python template ignores lib/)
#    vendor/  tgdrive/web/vendor/pdfjs is a bundled, tracked dependency
#    bin/     generic enough to catch real scripts
#    data     a bare "data" catches linux-setup/pc/data and pcctl/gui/data
#    *.dat    upower test fixtures use it
#    secrets.*  would hide src/pcctl/core/secrets.py
#    package-lock.json / lockfiles  are committed on purpose (reproducible installs)
#
#  Already-committed files are NOT affected by this file. To stop tracking one:
#    git rm -r --cached <path>   then commit.
# ============================================================================


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 1. SECRETS & CREDENTIALS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep this section at the top: leaking any of these is the costliest mistake.

# Environment files. Templates (.env.example / .env.sample) stay tracked (see the end).
.env
.env.*
*.env
.envrc
.direnv/

# Google OAuth (yt-subs-* tools) and other API tokens
client_secret*.json
token_*.json
credentials.json
service-account*.json
*-credentials.json

# Generic secret stores
secrets.json
secrets.yaml
secrets.yml
secrets.toml
.secrets/
*.secret

# Private keys, certificates, keystores
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
*.jks
*.keystore
*.kdbx
id_rsa*
id_ecdsa*
id_ed25519*
*.gpg
*.asc

# Per-user auth files some tools drop into a project folder
.netrc
.pgpass
.htpasswd

# Telegram client sessions (Telethon / Pyrogram). These are full logins.
*.session
*.session-journal

# WhatsApp Web automation sessions (whatsapp-web.js / Baileys)
.wwebjs_auth/
.wwebjs_cache/
auth_info*/


# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
# 2. OPERATING SYSTEMS
# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Linux: editor backups, file-manager metadata, NFS temp files, trash
*~
.fuse_hidden*
.directory
.Trash-*
.nfs*

# macOS: Finder metadata, resource forks, Spotlight/Time Machine folders
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble
.LSOverride
._*
.Spotlight-V100
.Trashes
.fseventsd
.TemporaryItems
.VolumeIcon.icns
.DocumentRevisions-V100
.com.apple.timemachine.donotpresent

# Windows: thumbnail caches, folder settings, shortcuts, recycle bin
Thumbs.db
Thumbs.db:encryptable
ehthumbs.db
ehthumbs_vista.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
*.stackdump


